3.
ZONING: BASIC STANDARDS & USES
- The suitabillty of the subject property for development
according to the standards and uses of the existing zoning district, compared to the suitabillty of the
subject property for development according to the standards and uses of the proposed zoning
district.
Current Zoning
The property is more suitable to develop or redevelop
under MUB zoning standards than County MU
standards. The subject property is proposed to be
annexed into the City of Cheyenne, which would
require a City zoning designation. The subject
property currently does not have access to City
services in the form of water or sewer, which
prompted the property owners to annex into the City
of Cheyenne. The zoning designation of MUB most
closely matches the County zoning designation of MU
and will ensure the property is cohesive with the
surrounding City MUB zone.
4.
STREETS & OPEN SPACE
- The abillty of the subject property and surrounding vicinity to be developed
according to the Subdivision Standards in Article 4 considering the proposed zoning.
The applicant is seeking to rezone the land as is. Any additional lot requirements regarding the
use of the parcel will be addressed in the site plan review process. The subject properties are at
the intersection of two prominent arterials with a largely built-out street network.
5.
ZONING: INTENT, APPLICABILITY, & DESIGN OBJECTIVES
- The ability of the appilcation to support the
Intent and Applicability statements ofthe proposed zoning district, and achieve the Desi’n Objectives
ofany specific standards.
The MUB zone is intended to have a diverse mix of uses in a compact development pattern. The
subject property is adjacent to an area zoned MUB with a diverse array of uses that exemplify the
intent of the District. Any development or redevelopment at this location will complement the
surrounding uses and be required to meet the design objectives of the MUB zone. The MUB zone
will ensure quality development that compliments the surrounding character on a prominent
corner in the City, furthering the intent of the MUB district.
